      "message": "In et171\\_flash.cc (RunFlashFw), a pointer to a local file stream is handed to the brom object:\n\n```c\nbrom.SetRawCmdDump(\u0026raw_cmd_fw_file);\n\n```\n\nWhile brom effectively goes out of scope soon after RunFlashFw returns, leaving a pointer to a destroyed local variable inside a longer-lived object (brom is allocated in main()) is an anti-pattern.\n\n**Remediation:** Clear the pointer right before exiting RunFlashFw (brom.SetRawCmdDump(nullptr);), or better yet, move the file management strictly inside the BootromComm class.",
