      "message": "In et171\\_flash.cc (RunFlashCmd), the size of the wrapped command is extracted directly via std::memcpy:\n\n```c\nuint32_t wrapped_cmd_size \u003d 0;\nstd::memcpy(\u0026wrapped_cmd_size, \u0026firmware[done + 2], sizeof(uint32_t));\n\n```\n\nThis fails entirely if the host tool is compiled on a big-endian architecture. You correctly handle endianness elsewhere via ReadLittleEndian.\n\n**Remediation:** Use your utility function for consistency and safety:\n\n```c\nauto size_opt \u003d ReadLittleEndian\u003cuint32_t\u003e(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e(\u0026firmware[done + 2], 4));\nif (!size_opt) { /* handle error */ }\nuint32_t wrapped_cmd_size \u003d size_opt.value();\n\n```",
